<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14033" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Dindymus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-os</span></b> ), i, m., and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Dindy-mon</span></b> ,
		i, n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δίνδυμον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a mountain in Mysia near Pessinus, sacred to
			Cybele</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 5, 32, 40, § 142</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Prop. 3</span></i>
			(4), 22, 3; <i><span class="en">Cat. 63, 91</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. F. 4,
				249</span></i>.—Also, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Dindyma</span></b> , ōrum,
				n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δίνδυμα, τά</span>,
				<i><span class="en">Verg.
				A. 9, 618</span></i>; <i><span class="en">10, 252</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 2,
				223</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. F. 4, 234</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Dindymēnē</span></b> ,
				ēs, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δινδυμηνή</span>, <i>the goddess
				Cybele, who was worshipped there</i>, <i><span class="en">Hor. C. 1,
				16, 5</span></i>.—<i>Gen.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Dindymenae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cat.
					63, 13</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Dindy-mārĭus</span></b> ,
				ĭi, m., <i>a
				priest of Cybele</i>, <i><span class="en">Commod. 17,
			6</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
